# --- Encoding & line-ending policy (see Test/pack20/entryEncodingImmunity.test.js) ---
#
# `index.html` has been damaged twice by a legacy-ANSI round trip:
# PowerShell 5.1 `Get-Content` defaults to the system ANSI codepage (cp1251),
# then `Set-Content -Encoding UTF8` writes UTF-8. Every non-ASCII character gets
# double-encoded (mojibake) and a BOM is added. Player-visible symptoms were the
# loading splash showing `Р—РђР“Р РЈР—РљРђвЂ¦` and the supercomputer icon turning
# into a broken glyph instead of 🖥.
#
# `index.html` is now 100% ASCII (text -> numeric character references, raw-text
# zones and comments -> transliteration). ASCII bytes are identical in UTF-8 and
# cp1251, so any such round trip is byte-for-byte a no-op. Pack 20 enforces this.
#
# Line endings: index.html / style.css / game.js are authored with LF. `text=auto`
# keeps normalisation consistent across machines instead of relying on the local
# `core.autocrlf` setting.
index.html	text=auto eol=lf
style.css	text=auto eol=lf
game.js		text=auto eol=lf

# Other source files: normalise line endings, no per-file EOL override.
*.js		text=auto eol=lf
*.json		text=auto eol=lf
*.md		text=auto eol=lf
*.sh		text eol=lf
*.cjs		text=auto eol=lf
*.mjs		text=auto eol=lf
*.py		text=auto eol=lf
*.yml		text=auto eol=lf
*.yaml		text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png		binary
*.jpg		binary
*.jpeg		binary
*.gif		binary
*.webp		binary
*.ico		binary
*.woff		binary
*.woff2		binary
*.ttf		binary
*.otf		binary
*.mp3		binary
*.ogg		binary
*.wav		binary
